From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:14:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 35/41] usb: xhci-mtk: resume the controller before shutdown

A runtime-suspended controller has its clocks disabled. xhci_shutdown()
then accesses registers of a gated block. Resume the controller first.
Skip the shutdown when the resume fails.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
index ed7e17e1a72e..61e99114bf9f 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
@@ -741,6 +741,10 @@ static void xhci_mtk_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct xhci_hcd_mtk *mtk = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct usb_hcd *hcd = mtk->hcd;
 
+	/* Runtime suspend gates the clocks: resume before register access. */
+	if (pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev) < 0)
+		return;
+
 	if (hcd->driver->shutdown)
 		hcd->driver->shutdown(hcd);
 }
